jobDescription:
Position overview: The Senior Group Manager – Product Marketing will lead Intuitive India's Product Marketing vertical, spanning our Robotic-Assisted Surgery (RAS) platforms and our expanding Digital Solutions portfolio. This is a high-visibility, mission-critical leadership role at the intersection of customer insight, commercial strategy, and stakeholder influence. As a core member of the Marketing Leadership team, this individual will define portfolio strategy, lead go-to-market execution, and drive adoption and value validation for our growing product suite — including the imminent launches of our latest and most advanced robotic surgery platforms such as the da Vinci 5 and da Vinci Single Port in India.&#xa0; Working closely with global, regional, and country teams, the Senior Group Manager will shape the commercial and clinical narrative for robotic-assisted surgery in India, building a legacy of meaningful impact on how care is delivered to patients across the country. This is an ideal opportunity for a marketing leader who wants to build and influence at a national level — someone energised by complex problem-solving, cross-functional leadership, and creating lasting clinical and economic impact in healthcare. Roles and

RESPONSIBILITIES:
Portfolio Strategy &amp; Go-to-Market Develop and execute strategic marketing plans for the da Vinci platform and digital portfolio in alignment with company priorities and commercial objectives. Define Intuitive India's portfolio positioning and manage the full product lifecycle — from launch readiness and adoption to utilisation and value validation. Lead market segmentation, competitive landscape analysis, and deep customer discovery to identify growth opportunities and inform commercial strategy. Drive go-to-market planning for new product introductions, including the da Vinci 5 and SP launches, ensuring seamless coordination across commercial, clinical, and training functions. Customer &amp; KOL Engagement Build and sustain relationships with key opinion leaders (KOLs), surgical societies, and strategic hospital accounts to drive clinical advocacy and gather market insights. Serve as a visible marketing leader at national conferences, surgical symposia, live procedure broadcasts, and key industry events. Translate clinical and economic evidence into compelling value propositions and messaging that resonate across surgeon, hospital, and administrative stakeholders. Team Leadership &amp; Culture Lead and develop a team of marketing professionals, setting a high bar for strategic thinking, commercial execution, and cross-functional collaboration. Build a team culture grounded in data-driven decision-making, thought leadership, and a strong bias for action. Mentor and grow team members, creating clear development pathways and a shared sense of mission. Commercial Excellence &amp; Analytics Establish a discipline of measuring the impact and return on all marketing investments, with structured KPIs and performance reporting to leadership. Leverage data and market analytics to surface actionable insights, refine strategy, and communicate results through compelling executive-level storytelling. Manage marketing budgets with rigour, ensuring resource allocation is tied to commercial priorities and measurable outcomes. Cross-Functional &amp; Global Collaboration Partner with sales, clinical affairs, regulatory, public affairs, and global marketing teams to drive product innovation, compliance, and market readiness. Collaborate with Intuitive's Asia regional and global corporate teams to adapt and localise marketing strategies for the Indian market context. Proactively identify new partnerships and opportunities to expand Intuitive's reach, ecosystem value, and market presence in India. &#xa0;

